/*===============================================================================
📘 SYSTEMVERILOG ASSERTIONS — IMPLICATION OPERATOR
===============================================================================

🔹 1. WHAT IS IT?
The **implication operator** expresses a conditional timing rule: “If this happens, then that must follow.”

Syntax:
   sequence_exp |-> property_exp    // Overlapped
   sequence_exp |=> property_exp    // Non-overlapped

- LHS = Antecedent (“if” part)
- RHS = Consequent (“then” part)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 2. TYPES OF IMPLICATION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

| Type | Symbol | Starts Evaluation | Description |
|------|---------|-------------------|--------------|
| **Overlapped** | `|->` | Same clock cycle | RHS begins immediately when LHS is true |
| **Non-overlapped** | `|=>` | Next clock cycle | RHS begins from the following clock edge |

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 3. EXAMPLES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

✅ Overlapped (`|->`)
property p_overlap;
  @(posedge clk) valid |-> (a ##3 b);
endproperty
→ When valid is 1, check starts immediately; after 3 cycles b must be 1.


✅ Non-overlapped (|=>)
property p_non_overlap;
  @(posedge clk) valid |=> (a ##3 b);
endproperty
→ When valid is 1, check starts on next clock edge.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 4. REAL USE CASE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
property p_req_ack;
  @(posedge clk)
    $rose(req) |=> ##[1:3] ack;
endproperty

assert property(p_req_ack)
  else $error("ACK not received within 3 cycles after REQ");
✔ $rose(req) ensures the property triggers only once per request.
✔ ##[1:3] defines a timing window for ack to arrive.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 5. SUMMARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Implication links cause → effect conditions.
|-> → check starts same cycle (immediate response).
|=> → check starts next cycle (delayed response).
Used for: handshake, valid/ready, protocol timing, etc.

===============================================================================*/
